     "description": "As the popular story goes, the Daiquiri was invented around 1898 by American mining engineer Jennings Cox at the mines near the Cuban village of Daiquirí — though Cubans were drinking rum with lime and sugar long before that. The drink was made famous by El Floridita bar in Havana and its regular, Hemingway. A classic Daiquiri is not a frozen dessert but a lean, balanced sour that bartenders use to test each other: if the Daiquiri is good, you can trust the bar.",
