    "en": {
     "instructions": "Pour the gin, juice and syrup into an ice-filled glass, top up with soda and stir.",
     "description": "The Collins traces its lineage to John Collins, a waiter at London's Limmer's club in the early 19th century, while the name 'Tom' took hold after the New York hoax of 1874, when people were told that a certain Tom Collins was spreading rumors about them in the bar next door. Essentially it is a gin lemonade: a sour lengthened with soda. The IBA lists it today as the John Collins; the tall Collins glass is named after it.",
     "garnish": "lemon wheel, cocktail cherry",
     "origin": "United Kingdom / USA"
    }
