     "description": "A Jamaican punch known for its rhyming rule \"one of sour, two of sweet, three of strong, four of weak\" (sour, sweet, strong and weak in a 1:2:3:4 ratio). The link to planters and to the Planter's Hotel in St. Louis is more legend than fact, but the punch appears in print as early as the 1870s. Myers's rum long promoted it as its signature drink. There are countless recipes; what they share is dark rum, citrus, sugar and spice.",
