     "instructions": "Shake with ice and strain into a chilled glass.",
     "description": "Constantino Ribalaigua, the legendary bartender at Havana's El Floridita, made this version of the Daiquiri for Ernest Hemingway. The writer reportedly had diabetes and wanted no sugar, but loved double measures of rum — hence the drink's other name, Papa Doble. Grapefruit and maraschino make it drier and more complex than a regular Daiquiri, though modern versions still leave room for some sugar for balance.",
